84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Prolonged sedentary behavior contributes to discomfort and reduced productivity. This project introduces SitSense, an integrated system designed to encourage micro-exercise breaks through behavioral nudges. The system combines an ergonomic cushion with a pressure sensor, vibration motors and a software interface that monitors sitting time. SitSense prompts the user with a gentle physical prompt when a sitting limit is exceeded, while intelligently respecting the user's schedule by referencing their calendar. The design is based on behavioral change models. Evaluation confirmed high user willingness to adopt the product, validating the potential of combining interactive technology and ergonomics to encourage healthier daily habits.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
