126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Sitsense is an ergonomic pillow used to help users increase their motivation trough user experiences. To make it able to be used for a long period of time, it is key to use good cushioning and ergonomic shaping. Looking at the market, there is already a good amount of ergonomic pillows that help users have a good seating position during work. Our design goes a step further, including smart elements, such as limit switches inside the pillow that detect the use of the pillow, vibration motors in the pillow to nudge the user to stand up and take breaks in between work and lastly an app for computers, to set timers, see progress and get feedback on their use with the product. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The seat has a layer of soft cushioning, giving enough comfort while using, but also gives and opportunity for the product to detect the weight and use of the product through the limit switch underneath. To increase the users interaction and experiences with the product, we made it so that the product only works when a user sits on it, making them connect to their own product with intend. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The buzzers are used to inform users to take active breaks, by nudging them in an uncomfortable way. This is not optimal, as it might influence the experience of the user in a bad way, but we have used multiple other techniques in the service to make up for this potential loss, to make the user feel more connected to the product. The use of variety in pillow colors, ability to plan working hours or breaks themselves, and the overall simplicity of the product, so that it is integrated into their surroundings, boosting the effectiveness of the product experiences. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
