132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (Sitsense gives the opportunity for the user to upload their personal selected Google Calendar. This provides satisfactory benefits for the user, as they feel more integrated into the system of the product by having their own input, even though the algorithm of the app will decide when breaks should happen, according the 45 minute timer. Next to it is the limit switch inside the ergonomic pillow, which is used to measure the actual interaction of the user taking part of the user experience, sitting down when the timer is active and standing up when the timer runs out. When the Sitsense detects the user standing up to take a break, another timer will run, this time to collect the time the product is not in use. When the user comes back from their break, this time is stored in an Excel document, stored locally on the device, which is used by the interface to collect and give feedback upon. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
