/E (The step of alligning a product that works as a solution for the problem was done through the product architecture that showed main features like sensor detection, in which detects the standing and the sitting of the user. it also showed the timer system which.described the 45 minutes interval. Other features in the product architecture helped to understand what features should be included in the product like feedback loop.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (This matches with the research by adressing the sedentary movements, encourages behavioural change through nudging, as well as supports autonomy and intrinsic motivation. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The real-time response to idleness and motion through vibration and on-screen prompts was the main part found with the data communication. Through simple icons, and mailny communicating the main data and storing it privately. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Taking the research done as an initial step in consideration, we carefully thought that the way to communicate our data worked as a gentle cues and a simple feedback to lower your stress instead of having additional digital fatigue. Moreoner, it emphasized gaining user trust and using autonomy.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The prototype significantly showed the potential of integrating ergonomics into interactive technology, to promote micro-exercise. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Overall the \(TAM\) indicated that the users generally find it easy to use and moderately useful.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [19]
>>
